{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>With the rivers</b>. He has now finished recounting the mighty acts of HaShem on behalf of Israel; now he begins to recount His might, in that He constantly seeks the land of Israel to water it, as David mentioned: \"You, O Elohim, send abundant rain\" — after it says \"the beasts dwell in it,\" and the might of YHWH is seen in every generation, at His command to bring rain. And it is written: \"who does great things,\" and after it: \"who gives rain.\" For one may wonder how the clouds rise from the rivers and likewise from the sea, like the one who calls to the waters of the sea, when the clouds rise from the sea and go to bring rain to the place that HaShem commands them. Therefore it is written: \"YHWH of hosts is His name, who pours them out.\"" "<b>Your horses</b> are the clouds that He assigns to bring rain upon the place of His desire. Do not wonder that He called them His horses, as in: \"Behold, YHWH rides upon a swift cloud.\" HaShem makes clouds His steed." "And the meaning of <b>salvation</b> is to bring salvation to the inhabitants of the land."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The phrase הנה ה' רוכב על עב is paraphrased; the closing citation 'וישפכם ה׳ צבאות שמו' does not correspond to any single biblical verse and may be Ibn Ezra's condensed paraphrase or a variant citation.", 1 "The last clause 'השם עבים רכובו' appears to paraphrase Psalm 68:34 ('רכבו על עבי שחקים'); the construction is compressed and the syntactic relationship between the two prooftexts is not fully articulated."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:10.655954612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}